Lab patch for Strix 685bbc8 (v1.7.1), applied at image build.

Why: two LiteLLM settings Strix has no switch for.
1. A model name with "llama-2", "llama-3" or a Cohere "command-r" in it makes LiteLLM
   fetch a tokenizer from huggingface.co when Strix counts tokens for compaction
   (strix/llm/context_budget.py 76-90 -> litellm/utils.py 2172-2209 at v1.101.0).
   disable_hf_tokenizer_download keeps counting on the bundled tiktoken encoding.
2. Ollama must serve every call with the experiment's pinned num_ctx. Strix has no
   setting for Ollama options, so LAB_OLLAMA_NUM_CTX sets LiteLLM's OllamaChatConfig,
   whose values go into options of every ollama_chat request
   (litellm/llms/ollama/chat/transformation.py 292-301 at v1.101.0).

diff --git a/strix/config/models.py b/strix/config/models.py
index 102d132c..26d55ebd 100644
--- a/strix/config/models.py
+++ b/strix/config/models.py
@@ -785,6 +785,15 @@ def _configure_litellm_compatibility() -> None:
     # Disabling streaming logging also disables that callback for streamed calls.
     litellm.disable_streaming_logging = False
     litellm.suppress_debug_info = True
+    # Lab patch: count tokens with the bundled tiktoken encoding only. Without this,
+    # a model name containing "llama-2", "llama-3" or a Cohere "command-r" makes
+    # LiteLLM download a tokenizer from huggingface.co (litellm/utils.py 2172-2209).
+    litellm.disable_hf_tokenizer_download = True
+    # Lab patch: send the experiment's pinned context window with every Ollama call
+    # (options.num_ctx), so Ollama never falls back to its own default.
+    num_ctx = os.environ.get("LAB_OLLAMA_NUM_CTX", "").strip()
+    if num_ctx:
+        litellm.OllamaChatConfig(num_ctx=int(num_ctx))
 
     _register_litellm_cost_callback()
     _install_openrouter_stream_cost_capture()
